WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:03.230
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie!

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.520
This week on Walking Dead we got a deep look
into Abraham’s group including Doctor Mullett

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.040
a huge teaser for Washington DC and more ominous
Sanctuary signs.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.450
Candy Bars, Comic Books and Easy Cheese for
everyone.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.490
Quick shout out if you’re finding me for
the first time.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:18.949
Each week I pick one random subscriber from
the comments on my review videos to give an

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:20.039
Amazon Gift Card too.

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:23.320
I’ll be announcing who that is tomorrow
in my Q&amp;A video.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.910
There will be a link to that at the end of
this video.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:30.679
So let’s talk about our top 5 WTF moments,
then I’ll do my review and list some of

00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:32.770
the biggest questions I had after watching.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.110
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:38.700
Number 5 - Smiley Face Abraham Luckiest Man
in the World.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.480
For people who haven’t read the comic book,
this scene was a crash course in Abraham.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.680
He’s got a plan just like the governor.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.830
But despite all the smiley faced Walker Smashing,
the tone of the moment and Tara’s reaction

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.300
were fairly positive.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.970
So I feel like the writers want us to trust
him.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.530
There were a couple moments later in the episode
that raised some red flags, but I’ll mention

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:57.560
them in a sec.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.580
Number 4 - Candy Bars, Comic Books and Crazy
Cheese.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.170
This is all about Michonne and Carl getting
to know each other again.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.760
Michonne has started to open up a lot more
about her past.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:11.310
And Carl has grown up or tried to grow up
really fast in the last couple of episodes.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:15.880
It’s a good opportunity for us to get Michonne
backstory.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:20.800
She’s pacing herself in how much she reveals
but I love the bond she and Carl have.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.200
She’s revealing things to him that she’s
never told anyone.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.200
And Carl opens up about Judith.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.920
They’re best friend like Rick wants, but
I think she also kind of thinks of him as

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.120
a little brother.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.870
Their scenes are a welcome aspirin pill to
the stress headache you get from Rick and

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.780
Carl yelling at each other.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.299
Number 3 - Who the eff is downstairs.

00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:38.870
I got a strong Hunters Vibe but since no one
got thrown on a grill I think they were just

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.750
supposed to be random survivors.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.420
Albeit really murdery randoms.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.890
There were enough WTF moments from the house
that I actually separated the most notable

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:47.890
ones.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.729
The first being their arrival and Rick darting
under the bed.

00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:54.062
Anyone who has hidden under the bed from someone
understands what it’s like when you see

00:01:54.062 --> 00:01:56.120
a pair of feet walk up.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:00.590
Number 2 - My bed now Jackoff.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.250
I was right there under the bed with Rick.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.190
I actually thought he was going to have to
pinch the guy’s nose shut and kill him in

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.000
order to keep from being discovered.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.830
He was still breathing and Jackoff number
1 probably would have straight up killed Rick

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.070
if he found out.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:16.480
Later he actually does kill one of the randoms,
but then the tension was all about him turning.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:17.560
Which he eventually did.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:22.510
I liked the twist of Rick being able to use
that to escape with Michonne and Carl.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.330
Number 1 - The fate of the human race depends
on Doctor Mullett.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:30.450
Abraham teases us that because Eugene might
now what caused the outbreak, potentially

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.730
there’s a cure.

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:35.640
This has been one of the biggest ongoing questions
of the comic book and the tv show.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.900
I’ve always thought the virus itself was
a red herring, something that didn’t really

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:39.900
matter.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.300
I think the real story of walking dead is
what happens to these regular people after.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.650
And making it about a ‘cure’ would completely
change the show.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:50.980
Everyone’s focus would be about the solution
and this is really supposed to be a drama

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:51.980
about people.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:52.980
Now it’s your turn.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:57.760
Let me know what you’re biggest WTF Moment
was from the episode and do you think the

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.410
show should ever reveal a cure?

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.710
Overall I loved the deep look at Abraham’s
group, the tease of Washington DC, Rick’s

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.890
game of hide and seek and the continuing sanctuary
teasers.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:11.660
I’m going to give the episode a solid B
plus, just because of all the new elements

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:15.340
that abraham’s group introduced to the story
and the hide and seek pacing.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.840
Things would go from super intense like Rick
staring into that guy’s eyes underneath

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.680
the bed and then they’re just easy breezy
easy cheesing their way down the rail road

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:23.680
tracks.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.060
I love the dynamic of Rick’s group now that
Michonne is with them.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.819
It just gives the writers opportunities for
more comedy and have those classic family

00:03:29.819 --> 00:03:31.420
breakfast moments.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:35.610
Rick and Carl might be doing better, but I
still see a lot of tension between them.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.150
Most of that now is over them thinking baby
Judith is dead.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:42.330
Here are a couple of important questions I
had during the episode.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:47.260
1 - Is the Crook road sign meant to imply
that Abraham is a Crook?

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:52.060
2 - Does Carl’s character genuinely hate
soy milk or were the writers just trolling?

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:55.010
3 - When are they going to run into Baby Judith
again?

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.010
Quick Side Note though.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:59.762
Both Tyreese’s group and Rick’s group
are headed toward the sanctuary, they’ll

00:03:59.762 --> 00:04:02.110
probably all get there before the end of the
season.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.950
4 - What was up with that mutilated painting?

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:08.040
Was it just meant to juxtapose the nice looking
one of the Rabbits?

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:12.050
I actually thought the Rabbit painting was
a visual mirror to Lizzie killing the rabbits

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.450
in episode 10.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:20.060
5 - Is Eugene Autistic or just really clumsy.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:23.730
Despite looking like a redneck, I’m totally
willing to believe he’s a real deal scientist

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.940
who can help.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:28.770
But the whole clumsy rifle scene kind of says
DO NOT trust anything you hear about this

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:29.770
man.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.510
and 6 - What is Abraham trying to atone for.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:34.820
Tara calls him out on the DC mission.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:38.430
I think it’s pretty clear he did something
during Iraq or Afghanistan that he wants to

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.430
balance out.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:42.340
Let’s try to answer all those questions
in the comments.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.610
It’s going to be a little while before the
show gives us explicit answers.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:49.970
Next week is Daryl and Beth and from the looks
of the teaser things are only getting worse

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:50.970
for them.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:54.551
Remember I’m selecting one random subscriber
from the comments to give this week’s gift

00:04:54.551 --> 00:04:55.551
card to.

00:04:55.551 --> 00:04:57.830
I’ll announce who it is in my Q&amp;A video
tomorrow.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:01.580
Right now click here to get last week’s
episode and click here for that Q&amp;A video.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.790
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:04.319
High Fives!

